14-
15-Every definition and result must use exact hypotheses and local arguments. Sources document the mathematical and physical context; a citation is not a proof supplier in active physics content. A locally authored theorem must prove its stated implication from the declared mathematical premises and physical postulates. A formal perturbation series is coefficientwise algebra and carries no convergence claim. A regulator result is not a continuum result. An established theorem whose proof is not written locally is an authoring obligation, not an open problem. Genuinely unresolved claims use an op- item, receive a dated formulation/status/source review, and never become logical suppliers.
