items/lem-emx-unit-sphere-radial-flux.md:102:[F4] In the Statement, the standard embedded smooth structure is the atlas with charts $U_{i,\varepsilon}=\{p\in S^2:\varepsilon p_i>0\}$, for $i\in\{1,2,3\}$ and $\varepsilon\in\{-1,1\}$, whose coordinates delete $p_i$ and whose inverse inserts $p_i=\varepsilon\sqrt{1-\sum_{j\ne i}u_j^2}$ on the open unit disk. These charts cover $S^2$. For $t>0$, $(\sqrt t)'=(2\sqrt t)^{-1}$, and induction gives $(d/dt)^m\sqrt t=c_m t^{1/2-m}$ with $c_0=1$ and $c_{m+1}=(1/2-m)c_m$; thus the square root, and hence each chart transition on its positive-argument domain, is smooth. The charts give $T_pS^2=\{v\in\mathbb R^3:p\cdot v=0\}$; the stated outward orientation declares $(v,w)$ positive when $p\cdot(v\times w)>0$, and the displayed $\omega$ is its area form. [[def-smooth-differential-k-form]] defines smooth forms; [[thm-heine-borel-rn]] makes $S^2$ compact; and [[prop-integration-over-an-oriented-embedded-submanifold]] defines the integral of a compactly supported form on the oriented sphere through its embedding.
