items/pthm-em-uniform-ohmic-modal-decay.md:110:3.1 [Smooth PEC cavity: modal system, variational equations and uniqueness] Assume the full Axiom of Choice as in [F3]. Let $H\times M$ be the energy class of steps 1.2, with $M=\overline{\operatorname{span}\{w_j\}}\oplus K_M$. For coefficients $a_j=(\cdot,u_j)$, $b_j=(\cdot,w_j)$ declare the first-order modal system $a_j'=v^2\sqrt{\lambda_j}\,b_j-\gamma a_j$, $b_j'=-\sqrt{\lambda_j}\,a_j$ for $\lambda_j>0$, and $a_j'=-\gamma a_j$ for the electric zero modes, and declare the magnetic kernel data constant, $(B,K_M)'=0$ for every kernel test. Endow the paired-magnetic space with the completion $D_M$ of finite $w_j$-sums plus $K_M$ for the norm $\|w\|_{D_M}^2:=\|w\|_2^2+\|\operatorname{curl}w\|_2^2$, and consider the weak variational equations $\langle E_t,\phi\rangle=v^2\langle B,\operatorname{curl}\phi\rangle-\gamma\langle E,\phi\rangle$ for $\phi\in V$ and $\langle B_t,\psi\rangle=-\langle E,\operatorname{curl}\psi\rangle$ for $\psi\in D_M$. Then every initial pair in $H\times M$ has a unique $C(\mathbb R;H\times M)$ solution of this declared realization, it satisfies the modal equations distributionally, and finite electric and paired-magnetic modal sums together with the static kernel component converge uniformly on compact time intervals in energy norm. Existence and uniqueness are finite-dimensional: each paired system is a globally Lipschitz constant-coefficient system solved by [F7], and the kernel data are constant, so a candidate solution is the norm-limit of its finite modal sums; the sums converge because the energy $\sum_j(\varepsilon|a_j|^2+\mu^{-1}|b_j|^2)$ is controlled as in step 2.1 and the kernel component is retained exactly. Each finite sum with the static kernel satisfies the first-order equations distributionally in the interior: $\operatorname{curl}w_j=\sqrt{\lambda_j}u_j$ follows from [F3], while the electric zero eigenfields and magnetic kernel have zero curl. Uniform compact-time $L^2$ convergence passes these linear equations to the limit against compactly supported smooth spacetime tests by Cauchy–Schwarz [F5]. For the variational equations, the finite sums satisfy them against finite spectral tests by the full-$X$ identity of [F3], and the density of the finite spectral tests in $V$ and in $D_M$ passes the identities to the limit by Cauchy–Schwarz [F5], since uniform energy convergence on compact times controls both pairings. Conversely, testing the variational equations against $u_j$ (for $\phi$) and $w_j$ or kernel vectors (for $\psi$) recovers the modal equations, so the weak realization and the modal system are equivalent in the stated class; uniqueness follows from the scalar ODE uniqueness and the complete decomposition of step 1.2. For strong first-order solutions with $E\in C^1_tH\cap C_tV$ and $B\in C^1_tL^2\cap C_tH(\operatorname{curl})$, the same pairing gives $a_j'=v^2(B,\operatorname{curl}u_j)-\gamma a_j$ and, differentiating with $B'=-\operatorname{curl}E$ and the full-$X$ identity, $a_j''+\gamma a_j'+v^2\lambda_j a_j=0$ with $a_j'=-\gamma a_j$ at $\lambda_j=0$. No maximal rough tangential-trace realisation is claimed. [step 1.2, F3, F5, F7]
