items/pthm-fd-px06-prediction.md:37:    locator: Stokes sphere solution and drag.
items/pthm-fd-px06-prediction.md:57:Among classical pairs solving the same Stokes system, boundary condition and far-field limits, this pair is unique in the uniform decay class $u-U=O(r^{-1})$, $\nabla u=O(r^{-2})$, $p-p_\infty=O(r^{-2})$, with all bounds uniform in direction and pressure normalized by its limit. The classical regularity is $u\in C^2$, $p\in C^1$ locally up to $S_a$. Under SI units, $a,r,x$ are metres, $U$ is $\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$, $\rho_0$ is $\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}$, $\mu$ is $\mathrm{Pa\,s}$, $\nu$ is $\mathrm{m^2\,s^{-1}}$, pressure is pascals, and resultant is newtons. This is an exact zero-inertia model result; no error estimate comparing it with the full momentum equation retaining material acceleration, and no exterior Navier–Stokes existence claim, is asserted.
