items/prop-fd-pressure-gauge-observables.md:46:Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\in\{2,3\}$ and let $D\subset\mathbb R^d$ be a nonempty bounded connected Lipschitz open set, with $V=H^1_0(D;\mathbb R^d)$ and $Q=L^2_0(D)$. Take $g\in L^2(D;\mathbb R)$ and define $S_g(q):=\int_Dgq\,dx$ for $q\in Q$; this is a bounded pressure sensor. Put $\bar g:=|D|^{-1}\int_Dg\,dx$. On the normalized pressure space, $S_g=S_{g-\bar g}$. Whenever $p$ denotes an unnormalized pressure representative in a weak pressure term or sensor reading below, take $p\in L^2(D;\mathbb R)$; a normalized pressure is denoted $q\in Q\subset L^2(D;\mathbb R)$. The weak Stokes pressure term $-\int_Dp\,\operatorname{div}v\,dx$ is unchanged by $p\mapsto p+c$ for $v\in V$ and $c\in\mathbb R$. The unnormalized sensor reading $\int_Dgp\,dx$ is unchanged under every pressure shift $p\mapsto p+c$ if and only if $\int_Dg\,dx=0$, equivalently $g\in Q$.
