items/def-qftx-chiral-anomaly-interface.md:60:The only local BRST obstruction statement recorded here is a separate formal result for the specific Abelian jet complex used by the mathematical supplier, not a BRST construction for the general Lie algebra $\mathfrak g$ above. In the convention of `def-qftx-brst-relative-local-cohomology`, a compactly supported local horizontal $p$-form is a finite sum of $f_{i_1\ldots i_p}(x,z)\,dx^{i_1}\wedge\cdots\wedge dx^{i_p}$, with each coefficient smooth and compactly supported in $x\in\mathbb R^4$ and polynomial in finitely many field-jet coordinates $z^i_\alpha$; $i$ indexes the field and ghost generators and $\alpha$ their derivative multi-indices. Its total derivative is $D_\mu=\partial/\partial x^\mu+\sum_{i,\alpha}z^i_{\alpha+e_\mu}\partial_L/\partial z^i_\alpha$, where $e_\mu$ is the unit multi-index and $\partial_L$ is the left graded derivative; $d_H=dx^\mu\wedge D_\mu$. The differential $s$ is the odd ghost-number-one Abelian derivation fixed by `def-qftx-abelian-local-brst`, with $sa_\mu=\partial_\mu c_{\mathrm{gh}}$, $sc_{\mathrm{gh}}=0$, $s\bar c=B$, $sB=0$, and $s\psi=igc_{\mathrm{gh}}\psi$, extended by the graded Leibniz rule and commutation with spacetime derivatives; $a_\mu,\psi,B$ are even, $c_{\mathrm{gh}},\bar c$ are odd, and their ghost numbers are $0,0,0,1,-1$, respectively. On a horizontal $p$-form $\omega$, use $s\omega=(-1)^p s_{\mathrm{coeff}}\omega$, where $s_{\mathrm{coeff}}$ is this coefficient derivation. Thus $s^2=d_H^2=0$ and $sd_H+d_Hs=0$, with nilpotence of $s$ established by `lem-qftx-brst-nilpotence-doublets`. Write $\Omega^{r,p}_{\mathrm{loc},c}$ for the space of these forms homogeneous of ghost number $r\in\mathbb Z$ and form degree $0\le p\le4$, and set it to zero outside that form-degree range. For each order $n\ge1$, let $\mathcal K_n=\bigoplus_{r,p}\mathcal K_n^{r,p}$ be a bigraded subspace with $\mathcal K_n^{r,p}\subseteq\Omega^{r,p}_{\mathrm{loc},c}$ that is stable in the sense that $s(\mathcal K_n^{r,p})\subseteq\mathcal K_n^{r+1,p}$ and $d_H(\mathcal K_n^{r,p})\subseteq\mathcal K_n^{r,p+1}$. The relative class is the quotient
items/def-qftx-chiral-anomaly-interface.md:62:The direct supplier `prop-qftx-anomaly-obstruction` is a draft proposition with a supplied conditional proof. Its scalar construction premise is the draft theorem `thm-qftx-scalar-eg-induction`: under the Axiom of Choice (every family of nonempty sets has a choice function) and Countable Choice (every sequence of nonempty sets has a choice function), and for admissible flat scalar free data and a local scalar polynomial class as defined by `def-qftx-local-time-ordered-system`, that theorem asserts existence of symmetric multilinear time-ordered maps satisfying its contract at every finite order, with finite graph scaling bounds and local extension ambiguities. It asserts no convergence, adiabatic limit, positivity, or Ward identity. The exact statement of `prop-qftx-anomaly-obstruction` assumes those data and a time-ordering scheme satisfying that theorem. For each ghost number $r$, define the local-functional quotient $\mathscr F_n^r:=\mathcal K_n^{r,4}/d_H\mathcal K_n^{r,3}$ and put $\mathscr F_n^\bullet=\bigoplus_r\mathscr F_n^r$. The formal series module is $\mathscr F_n^\bullet\llbracket\hbar\rrbracket$, where $\hbar$ is a formal indeterminate. For some $n\ge1$, it further assumes an odd formal ghost-number-one operator $\mathcal W_\hbar=s+\sum_{j\ge1}\hbar^j\mathcal W_j$ on this module, $\mathcal W_\hbar^2=0$, and an element $X\in\mathscr F_n^0\llbracket\hbar\rrbracket$ with $\mathcal W_\hbar X=\hbar^n\mathcal A+O(\hbar^{n+1})$, where $O(\hbar^{n+1})$ denotes terms of formal degree at least $n+1$, all lower coefficients vanish, and $\mathcal A=[a_4]_{\mathscr F_n}$ for compactly supported $a_4\in\mathcal K_n^{1,4}$. It requires $\mathcal K_n^{0,4}$ to be exactly the admissible local counterterm densities. Under these hypotheses, that proposition states that $s a_4$ is $d_H$-exact and that there exists an admissible $b_4\in\mathcal K_n^{0,4}$ such that shifting $X$ by $-\hbar^n[b_4]_{\mathscr F_n}$ cancels the order-$n$ breaking if and only if $[a_4]_{s|d_H}=0$. This is used only in the stated conditional form: it does not establish that the hypotheses hold for the representation data above or construct a physical effective action, and it does not prove a quantum action principle.
