items/rem-fd-global-regularity-open.md:40:As checked on 2026-10-23, the Clay Mathematics Institute lists the three-dimensional Navier–Stokes existence-and-smoothness problem among its Active problems. In its announcement dated 2026-09-11, CMI said it contemplated an announcement that the problem had apparently been settled and that the evaluation process was deliberately unhurried. This remark records CMI's public status only: it does not assess or accept the announced proof, and this batch's two-dimensional periodic theorem makes no claim about three-dimensional Navier–Stokes or unrestricted three-dimensional Euler regularity.
