items/ex-nrqm-light-matter-two-level-dipole-drive-check.md:158:2.1 [Exact Coulomb and dipole compressions] All off-diagonal energy entries vanish by oddness in $x_1$, since the Laplacian and radial Coulomb multiplier preserve that parity. The derivative identity $\partial_jg_a=-x_jg_a/a^2$, integration by parts from [F7], and the Gaussian moments give $\int|\nabla w_\downarrow|^2=3/(2a^2)$ and $\int|\nabla w_\uparrow|^2=5/(2a^2)$. Explicitly $\partial_jw_\uparrow=-(\sqrt2/a)(\delta_{j1}-x_1x_j/a^2)g_a$; the line recurrence obtained by integrating $(x_1^{2n-1}e^{-x_1^2/a^2})'$ gives $\int x_1^4\rho=3a^4/4$, while product integration gives $\int x_1^2x_2^2\rho=\int x_1^2x_3^2\rho=a^4/4$, which yields the second gradient value. Polar integration gives $\int\rho/|x|=2/(\sqrt\pi a)$ and $\int |w_\uparrow|^2/|x|=4/(3\sqrt\pi a)$: spherical symmetry assigns one third of $\int |x|\rho=2a/\sqrt\pi$ to $\int x_1^2\rho/|x|$, and the radial integrals follow by substituting $u=r^2/a^2$. Therefore $\langle H_\kappa w_\downarrow,w_\downarrow\rangle=3\hbar^2/(4\mu a^2)-2\kappa/(\sqrt\pi a)$ and $\langle H_\kappa w_\uparrow,w_\uparrow\rangle=5\hbar^2/(4\mu a^2)-4\kappa/(3\sqrt\pi a)$. The declared parameters satisfy $a=3\sqrt\pi\hbar^2/(5\mu\kappa)$, so these values are $-9\hbar^2/(20\mu a^2)=-\hbar\omega_0/2$ and $+9\hbar^2/(20\mu a^2)=+\hbar\omega_0/2$. Every diagonal dipole entry vanishes by coordinate parity, and $\langle D_1w_\downarrow,w_\uparrow\rangle=(q\sqrt2/a)\int x_1^2\rho=qa/\sqrt2=d$; its reverse equals it by real symmetry. The cross entries for $D_2,D_3$ are zero by oddness in $x_2,x_3$. Thus the actual compressions are exactly $H_a=(\hbar\omega_0/2)\sigma_z$, $D_1^W=d\sigma_x$, $D_2^W=D_3^W=0$. [given, F6, F7, step 1.1, algebra]
items/cex-nrqm-uncertainty-commutator-zero-on-a-core-is-not-spectral-compatibility.md:56:[F2] **The trace and integration by parts.** $H^{1}(0,L)$ consists of the classes with an $L^{2}$ weak derivative, each class has a continuous absolutely continuous representative $u^{*}$ with $\int_{0}^{L}u\overline{v'}=u^{*}(L)\overline{v^{*}(L)}-u^{*}(0)\overline{v^{*}(0)}-\int_{0}^{L}u'\overline v$ for $u,v\in H^{1}(0,L)$; a compactly supported smooth function vanishes near the endpoints, so $C^{\infty}_{c}(0,L)\subseteq D_{\theta}$ for every $\theta$ ([[def-nrqm-intervals-hilbert-sobolev-spaces]], [[lem-nrqm-intervals-integration-by-parts]] clauses (a),(b)).
