items/pthm-fd-px08-prediction.md:55:Let $\rho_0,\mu>0$, $\nu=\mu/\rho_0$, and $U\in\mathbb R$. Use SI units: length metres, time seconds, velocity $U,A$ in $\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$, density $\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}$, viscosity $\mathrm{Pa\,s}$, diffusivity $\nu$ in $\mathrm{m^2\,s^{-1}}$, periods $L_x,L_y,L_z$ in metres, and $k$ in $\mathrm{m^{-1}}$. For Cartesian fields use $\operatorname{div}u=\partial_xu_x+\partial_yu_y+\partial_zu_z$ and componentwise $\Delta u$. For $t>0,y>0$ and $x,z\in\mathbb R$, set $I_0=\int_0^\infty e^{-r^2}dr$, $E(s)=I_0^{-1}\int_s^\infty e^{-r^2}dr$ for $s\ge0$, and $u(t,x,y,z)=(UE(y/(2\sqrt{\nu t})),0,0)$, with constant pressure. This field is smooth for positive time and positive $y$, solves unsteady Stokes and full constant-density Navier–Stokes because its convective term vanishes, has vector wall trace $(U,0,0)$ for $t>0$, tends to zero as $y\to\infty$, and tends to zero as $t\downarrow0$ for each fixed $y>0$. The corner $(t,y)=(0,0)$ is excluded. For $0<\varepsilon<1$,
