items/lem-em-newtonian-linkage-symmetry.md:197:Hunter §2.6.1 and §2.7, printed pp. 33-37, treat the Newtonian potential of compactly supported data and its local kernel estimates; Teschl §5.3, equations (5.21)-(5.26), printed pp. 117-118, records the fundamental solution and the local integrability of the kernel. Neither text states the linkage pairing $B(u,v)$ or its symmetry; the statement and its proof assemble the two cited representations with the Tonelli/Fubini machinery of the measure-theory pages. The kernel normalization $\omega_2=4\pi$ used for the $n=3$ specialization is computed here from the chart-surface-measure convention, the unit-ball volume formula and the Gamma functional equation rather than quoted as a numerical convention.
