items/thm-fd-collision-maxwellian.md:89:6.1 For the profile obtained in step 5.1, $A=B$ on every elastic quadruple because its logarithm is a constant plus a linear and a quadratic collision invariant. The Definition's weak identity for each compactly supported smooth test therefore gives $\int\varphi Q_\nu(f(x,\cdot))\,dv=0$; the collision integrand also vanishes, so $D_x=0$. Conversely, the same calculation applies to every profile of this form, with weak annihilation conditional on its membership in $\mathcal D_\nu$. [F1, step 5.1, algebra] ∎
