items/ex-fd-x06-application.md:43:Assume $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$ and use the exact uniform-decay Stokes model for a sphere of radius $a=1\,\mathrm m$ with $\mu=1\,\mathrm{Pa\,s}$, $\rho_0=1\,\mathrm{kg\,m^{-3}}$, and uniform far-field velocity $U=(10^{-3},0,0)\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$. The exact model resultant with sphere normal directed into the fluid is $6\pi\cdot10^{-3}e_x\,\mathrm N$. Choose characteristic speed $U_{\rm ref}=|U|$ and length $L_{\rm ref}=a$, and define $\operatorname{Re}_a=\rho_0U_{\rm ref}L_{\rm ref}/\mu=10^{-3}$. This is only a parameter calculation and supplies no error estimate comparing this zero-inertia model with the full equation retaining material acceleration.
