items/texp-nrqm-kinematics-dirichlet-momentum-warning.md:136:[F1] **Interval Sobolev space and integration by parts.** $H^{1}(0,L)$ is the space of $L^{2}$ classes with an $L^{2}$ weak derivative; each class has a continuous representative, its trace $u^{*}$ is defined at the endpoints, and $-\int_{0}^{L}u\,\overline{v'} =u^{*}(0)\overline{v^{*}(0)}-u^{*}(L)\overline{v^{*}(L)}+\int_{0}^{L}u'\,\overline{v}$ for all $u,v\in H^{1}(0,L)$; the test classes $C_{c}^{\infty}(0,L)$ have zero endpoint traces and lie in $D(T)$ ([[def-nrqm-intervals-hilbert-sobolev-spaces]], [[lem-nrqm-intervals-integration-by-parts]]). Under the assumed Countable Choice, these test classes are dense in $L^{2}(0,L;\mathbb C)$ by [[lem-smooth-compactly-supported-functions-are-dense-in-ltwo-of-an-open-set]] applied to the open set $\Omega=(0,L)\subset\mathbb R$. In particular $D(T)\supseteq C_{c}^{\infty}(0,L)$ is dense in $L^{2}(0,L;\mathbb C)$ and $D(T)$ is a linear subspace of $H^{1}$.
items/texp-nrqm-kinematics-dirichlet-momentum-warning.md:146:**Proof technique:** direct; compute the adjoint of the Dirichlet momentum by integration by parts, show that no self-adjoint extension can keep the Dirichlet domain, test the Dirichlet functions against an arbitrary self-adjoint extension, and read the observability conclusion off the self-adjointness requirement of the observable postulate.
