items/ex-emg-xs-topological-charge.md:55:[F1] [[prop-emg-xs-rn-local-gauges]]: the current A-page item proves $\int_{S_r}\mathcal F=4\pi q_m$ and gives smooth local north/south potentials. Its proof is directly supplied using RN data, Hodge calculus and finite-chain Stokes.
items/ex-emg-xs-topological-charge.md:76:1.2 The conditional flux interface [L1] gives $\int_{S_r}\mathcal F_\beta=4\pi q\sin\beta\ne0$. By [L2], the unrotated field is a smooth source-free geometric electrovac datum on the full-sphere exterior, and its constant dual rotation is closed on the annulus. If $S_r=\partial c$ for a finite smooth singular 3-chain there, [F2] gives $\int_{S_r}\mathcal F_\beta=\int_c d\mathcal F_\beta=0$, a contradiction. A global smooth real one-form potential would likewise give zero flux by Stokes and $\partial S_r=0$. The north and south stereographic sphere charts, each omitting one pole, give product coordinate domains $\mathbb R\times(R_0,R_1)\times\mathbb R^2$, which are convex and hence star-shaped about any of their points. Pull back $\mathcal F_\beta$ to either domain, apply [L3] with $k=2$, and transport the resulting primitive back. This supplies smooth real patch potentials covering the annulus. Thus the KN sphere is nonbounding and its field is locally but not globally exact, conditionally on [L1-L2]. [L1, L2, L3, F2, A1, algebra]
items/ex-emg-xs-topological-charge.md:85:3.1 The RN conclusion follows from the current RN local-gauge proof and finite-chain Stokes. The KN conclusion remains conditional on the exact batch-21 flux, full-sphere verification and duality interfaces and their draft proofs. Neither yields a regular magnetic source or a quantization condition. [F1, F2, L1, L2, step 1.1, step 1.2, step 2.1] ∎
