items/ex-qft-x05.md:136:2.1 By [A2], $\mu_T(B)=\int_B\Gamma e^{-\Gamma t}\,d\ell(t)$ for Borel $B\subseteq[0,\infty)$. Taking $B=[0,\infty)$ gives total mass $1$, and the mean is $$\mathbb E[T]=\int_0^\infty t\Gamma e^{-\Gamma t}\,dt=\left[-t e^{-\Gamma t}\right]_0^\infty+\int_0^\infty e^{-\Gamma t}\,dt=\frac1\Gamma,$$ by integration by parts; $t e^{-\Gamma t}\to0$ since $\Gamma>0$. The survival function is continuous and strictly decreasing from $1$ to $0$, so the defining equation for $t_{1/2}$ has a unique solution; solving $e^{-\Gamma t_{1/2}}=1/2$ gives $t_{1/2}=\ln2/\Gamma$. These formulas use [A2], not the formal rate coefficient alone; no experiment or detector record is specified. [step 1.1, F3, F4, F5, F6, A1, A2, algebra] ∎
