items/lem-qft-dirac-covariance-spectrum.md:108:2.2 The test-generated subspaces are dense. For $u\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb R^3\setminus\{0\};\mathbb C^4)$, $P_\pm u$ is smooth and compactly supported away from the massless apex; such projected vectors are dense in $\mathcal H_\pm$ by [F1] and [F6], since removing the single point does not change an $L^2$ class. Choose $g\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb R)$ with $\int g(t)dt=1$ and set $\widehat F(t,\mathbf k)=g(t)W_D(-t,\mathbf k)u(\mathbf k)$. This is smooth and compactly supported in $(t,\mathbf k)$; its inverse spatial Fourier transform is Schwartz by repeated integration by parts. The definition in [F4] then gives $u_F=u$, and hence $P_\pm u_F=P_\pm u$. [F1, F4, F6, step 1.1, construct]
