items/ex-fd-single-mode-pressure.md:43:Assume Countable Choice and let $d\in\{2,3\}$, $A\in\mathbb R$, and $u(x)=A\sin(x_2)e_1$ on $Q_d$, where $e_1$ is the first coordinate vector. Then $u$ is smooth and divergence-free, $u\cdot\nabla u=0$, and its unique mean-zero pressure recovered by $Q(u\otimes u)$ is $\pi=0$. This is a verification of the pressure recovery map; it is not asserted to solve an unforced viscous Navier–Stokes equation.
