items/ex-em-parallel-plate-capacitor.md:91:1.1 Local integrability, classical relations and continuity: $E$ is bounded by $\sigma/\varepsilon_0$ and continuous off the two planes, so for every compactly supported smooth test the product $E\cdot\nabla\psi$ is compactly supported and the integral is finite; $\varphi$ is bounded by $\sigma h/\varepsilon_0$, hence locally integrable, and continuous because the slab formula, the two constants and the plane values match at $x_3=\pm h$. On each of the three open regions $E=-\nabla\varphi$ classically, with $|E|=\sigma/\varepsilon_0$ and normal direction inside the slab and $E=0$ outside; this is the regularity asserted in (a) and the uniform-field statement of (b). [F1, given]
items/lem-gr-hilbert-tensor-uniqueness.md:54:[L3] If $F$ is a continuous symmetric covariant $2$-tensor field on a chart domain $U$ and $\int_UF_{ab}q^{ab}w\,d^4x=0$ for every smooth symmetric compactly supported $q$, then $F=0$ on $U$ ([[lem-gr-compact-variation-coefficient-vanishing]], [[def-gr-metric-volume-form-and-current-flux]]).
items/lem-gr-hilbert-tensor-uniqueness.md:58:[L5] The integral of a compactly supported smooth top form over the oriented $M$ is additive and local: if the support of the form lies in a chart domain $U$, the integral equals the ordinary chart integral $\int_U f\,w\,d^4x$ ([[lem-finite-chart-localization-defines-choice-free-integration-and-compact-stokes]], [[def-smooth-manifold]]).
items/lem-gr-hilbert-tensor-uniqueness.md:68:3.1 (Coefficient vanishing on charts.) As $h$ ranges over all smooth symmetric compactly supported $(0,2)$-fields, $h^{ab}$ ranges over all smooth symmetric compactly supported $(2,0)$-fields by [L4]; equivalently, step 2.1 states $\int_MD_{ab}q^{ab}\mathrm{vol}_g=0$ for every smooth symmetric compactly supported $q$ written in covariant form. Fix a chart $(U,x)$ and restrict to $q$ supported in $U$; by [L5] the integral is the chart integral $\int_UD_{ab}q^{ab}w\,d^4x$. Since $D$ is smooth, hence continuous, [L3] gives $D=0$ on $U$. [step 2.1, L3, L4, L5]
items/post-tgrx-free-collapse-scattering.md:104:For each compact frequency interval $K=[\omega_-,\omega_+]\subset(0,\infty)$ with $\omega_-<\omega_+$, the packet Hilbert space is $\mathcal H_K=L^2(K,d\omega)$ with $\langle f,g\rangle_K:=\int_K\overline{f(\omega)}g(\omega)d\omega$. Write $C_c^\infty(K;\mathbb C)$ for zero extensions to $K$ of smooth functions compactly supported in $(\omega_-,\omega_+)$. A normalized packet is an $f\in C_c^\infty(K;\mathbb C)$ with $\int_K|f(\omega)|^2d\omega=1$; $f$ has units $\mathrm{s}^{1/2}$. For each $s\in\mathbb R$, the model supplies a bounded sesquilinear form $B_{\ell,s}:\mathcal H_K\times\mathcal H_K\to\mathbb C$, conjugate-linear in its first entry and linear in its second. Supply a single conjugate-linear outgoing map $A_{\ell,\rm out}:\mathcal D_+\to\mathfrak A$ with $[A_{\ell,\rm out}(f),A_{\ell,\rm out}(g)^*]=\langle f,g\rangle I$ and $[A_{\ell,\rm out}(f),A_{\ell,\rm out}(g)]=0$. Its restrictions to overlapping bands agree under zero extension. Define
items/pthm-em-electric-dipole-expansion.md:12:physical_scope: "The exterior potential of a compactly supported $L^1$ charge density in classical electrostatics: for $|x|\\ge2a$ the localised Newtonian potential equals the monopole term plus the dipole term plus an explicit remainder bounded by $16a^2\\|\\rho\\|_1/(4\\pi\\varepsilon_0|x|^3)$, uniformly in the exterior region. Only the potential is expanded; no derivative estimate of the remainder, no field expansion and no value on or inside the support are claimed."
