items/thm-nrqm-fock-and-equilibrium-fixed-n-coulomb-self-adjointness.md:110:1.1 [Global Hardy inequalities] Let $u\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb R^{3N})$ and fix a block index $i$ and a center $a\in\mathbb R^3$. For each fixed value of the remaining coordinates the slice $x_i\mapsto u(\dots,x_i,\dots)$ is a compactly supported smooth function on $\mathbb R^3$; [F2] gives $\int_{\mathbb R^3}|u|^2/|x_i-a|^2\,dx_i\le4\int_{\mathbb R^3}|\nabla_iu|^2dx_i$ for that slice, and integrating over the remaining coordinates by Tonelli [F3] with [F4] (translation to the center $a$) yields $\int|u|^2/|x_i-a|^2\le4\int|\nabla_iu|^2$. For a pair replace $(x_i,x_j)$ by the orthogonal coordinates $(y,z)$ of [F4]: then $|x_i-x_j|^2=2|y|^2$ and, applying the same slice argument in the $y$-variable to the transformed function, $\int|u|^2/|x_i-x_j|^2=\tfrac12\int|u'|^2/|y|^2\le2\int|\nabla_yu'|^2\le2\int(|\nabla_iu|^2+|\nabla_ju|^2)$. Both inequalities extend to all $u\in W^{1,2}(\mathbb R^{3N})$: choose $u_k\in C_c^\infty$ with $u_k\to u$ and $\nabla u_k\to\nabla u$ in $L^2$ ([F3]); the right-hand sides converge to the corresponding norms of $u$, while the left-hand sides are lower semicontinuous by Fatou along an a.e. convergent subsequence ([F3]). [F2, F3, F4, algebra]
