items/def-fd-bounded-stokes-observation-interface.md:39:Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\in\{2,3\}$ and let $D\subset\mathbb R^d$ be a nonempty bounded connected Lipschitz open set. Put $Q:=L^2_0(D)=\{q\in L^2(D;\mathbb R):\int_Dq\,dx=0\}$ with the $L^2$ norm, and write $Q'$ for the continuous real dual of $Q$. A bounded Stokes pressure sensor on $D$ is a bounded real-linear functional $S:Q\to\mathbb R$, where bounded means that its operator norm $\|S\|_{Q'}:=\sup_{\|q\|_{L^2(D)}\le1}|S(q)|$ is finite. The reading of $S$ at a normalized pressure $q\in Q$ is $S(q)$.
