items/pthm-tgrx-noether-horizon-entropy-variation.md:86:1.1 By [F4], the selected charge has the stated $W^c\xi_c$, $X^{cd}\nabla_{[c}\xi_{d]}$, $\mathbf Y(\mathcal L_\xi\phi)$, and exact-form decomposition. On $B$, $\xi=0$ and $\mathcal L_\xi\phi=0$. The $W^c\xi_c$ and $\mathbf Y$ terms and their field variations vanish there except for $\mathbf Y(\phi;\mathcal L_\xi\delta\phi)$. Covariance identifies this term with $\mathcal L_\xi\mathbf Y(\phi;\delta\phi)$; Cartan's formula [F2] writes it as $\iota_\xi d\mathbf Y+d(\iota_\xi\mathbf Y)$, whose pullback integrates to zero because $\xi=0$ on $B$ and $B$ has no boundary. The $dZ$ variation integrates to zero by Stokes [F3]. The Lagrangian ambiguity $\iota_\xi\mu$ vanishes on $B$, and the exact charge ambiguity also integrates to zero. Therefore $\delta\int_BQ_\xi=\delta\int_BX^{cd}\nabla_{[c}\xi_{d]}$. [A1, F1, F2, F3, F4, algebra]
