items/lem-emg-fx-symplectic-current-boundary.md:78:[A1] [[def-countable-choice]]: $\mathrm{AC}_\omega$ is the background assumption for the inherited smooth tangent and principal-connection convention; the exterior-calculus identities and finite-chain Stokes calculation use no further choice.
items/lem-nrqm-composites-exact-free-gaussian-propagation.md:136:7.1 [Operator standard deviations] For $\psi\in\mathcal S(\mathbb R)$ one has $U(P\psi)=M_pU\psi$ with $(M_pg)(p)=pg(p)$, because $\mathcal F_2(P\psi)(\xi)=\int_{\mathbb R}(-i\hbar\psi'(x))e^{-2\pi ix\xi}dx=2\pi\hbar\xi\,\mathcal F_2\psi(\xi)$ by integration by parts, the boundary terms $[\psi(x)e^{-2\pi ix\xi}]$ vanishing at $\pm\infty$ as $\psi\in\mathcal S(\mathbb R)$ [F6], and applying $D_\hbar$ with $p=2\pi\hbar\xi$ gives the claim [F2]; the unit vector $\psi_t$ of step 6.1 is the packet of steps 3.2 and 4.2, and for it this gives $b_t:=\langle P\psi_t,\psi_t\rangle=\langle UP\psi_t,U\psi_t\rangle=\int_{\mathbb R}p|U\psi_t(p)|^2dp=p_0$, a real number, and $\Delta P:=\|(P-b_t)\psi_t\|_2=\|U(P-b_t)\psi_t\|_2=\bigl(\int_{\mathbb R}(p-p_0)^2|U\psi_t(p)|^2dp\bigr)^{1/2}=\hbar/(2\sigma)$ by step 4.2, while $a_t:=\langle Q\psi_t,\psi_t\rangle=\int_{\mathbb R}x|\psi_t(x)|^2dx=c_t$ and $\Delta Q:=\|(Q-a_t)\psi_t\|_2=\bigl(\int_{\mathbb R}(x-c_t)^2|\psi_t(x)|^2dx\bigr)^{1/2}=\sigma\sqrt{1+\tau^2}$ by step 3.2; hence $\Delta Q\Delta P=\frac{\hbar}{2}\sqrt{1+\tau^2}$. [step 3.2, step 4.2, step 6.1, F2, F6, algebra]
