items/ex-fd-stokes-gradient-forcing-gauge.md:52:Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\in\{2,3\}$, let $D\subset\mathbb R^d$ be a nonempty bounded connected Lipschitz open set, and let $\nu>0$. Use $V=H^1_0(D;\mathbb R^d)$ with gradient norm and $Q=L^2_0(D)$. Define $\bar x_1:=|D|^{-1}\int_Dx_1\,dx$ and $\phi(x):=x_1-\bar x_1$. The load $F_\phi(v):=-\int_D\phi\,\operatorname{div}v\,dx$ is the gradient forcing $\nabla\phi=e_1$ in the weak sense. The unique weak Stokes solution is $(u,p)=(0,\phi)$, and the bounded gauge-invariant sensor $S_\phi(q):=\int_D\phi q\,dx$ has reading $S_\phi(p)=\int_D\phi^2\,dx>0$.
