items/thm-csm-frontier-ssep-heat-limit.md:102:The result is a mathematical deduction from the adopted finite stochastic model; it reports no measured diffusion and derives no Navier–Stokes equation from Newtonian mechanics. If one assigns a microscopic bond rate $1/\tau_0$ before the $N^2$ time acceleration and a physical lattice spacing $\ell_0/N$, then the accelerated rate is $N^2/\tau_0$ and the single-particle variance rate in each coordinate is $2(N^2/\tau_0)(\ell_0/N)^2=2\ell_0^2/\tau_0$. Thus the normalized coefficient $D=1$ corresponds to $D=\ell_0^2/\tau_0$ with physical units of length squared per time; this is a unit conversion for this chosen model.
