+# Batch 19 — Classical Non-Abelian Yang–Mills Model
+
+## Scope and plan comparison
+
+The assigned pair is qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model and its examples companion, order 975, in advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry, library physics. The canonical plan entry at research/plan-spec.json and the complete design section at research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md lines 261–273 agree on the page IDs, title, category, library, scope, required pages, and three planned physical item IDs. No design/plan conflict was found.
+
+The dated scaffold inventory's page_pairs row lists only qftx-gauge-geometry in requires; the canonical plan and current batch-19 manifest also require the published qft-c01 page. The plan and dispatch control, so batch 19 retains both page prerequisites. The scaffold's external supplier list names def-qft-framework-units and post-qft-constructed-model-and-measurement; only the former is used, for its exact four-dimensional natural-action normalization. The measurement postulate is not used: this carrier adopts a classical model with no matter, apparatus, measurement, or empirical premise.
+
+## Inspected prerequisite interfaces
+
+The current draft items def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data, def-qftx-principal-connection-form, def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket, lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi, and def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative were read. Current loadStep1Record / step1Decision rows bind the first three at level 0 and ready, the curvature/Bianchi lemma at level 1 and ready, and the associated covariant derivative at level 1 and ready. In particular, the curvature lemma's actual right-action convention is
+A_j = Ad_(g_ij^-1) A_i + theta_L(g_ij),
+F_i = dA_i + 1/2[A_i wedge A_i],
+and F_j = Ad_(g_ij^-1)F_i; it proves horizontality, equivariance, the sign relation to the imported vertical-valued curvature, and D_A F_A = 0 under AC_omega. Its complete current proof was inspected and matches the planned use. These draft carriers are current and ready; their draft status and pending prechecks are not prerequisite gaps.
+
+The published root mathematics interfaces def-gauge-group-of-a-smooth-principal-bundle and prop-gauge-transformations-act-on-principal-connections were read. A gauge transformation is a smooth equivariant bundle diffeomorphism over id_M; it acts by pushforward on horizontal distributions and transports vertical-valued curvature. The proof below uses local sections of a possibly nontrivial bundle and does not identify a global map M -> G with a gauge transformation.
+
+The published lem-sr-compact-variation-and-fundamental-lemma was read in full. Its compact-support integration-by-parts, parameter-differentiation, and scalar fundamental-lemma clauses apply in a Minkowski coordinate chart, choice-free. They support the Euler–Lagrange argument; the item still derives delta_A F_A = D_A delta A, the invariant-pairing integration identity, and the componentwise conclusion locally.
+
+## Source reading and harvested-result ledger
+
+Three independent full-text treatments were inspected for the A page. No retrieval failed, so no recovery retry or source_resolution disposition is required. All proofs in the authored carriers are local arguments; no source is used as a substitute for them.
+
+1. **Matthijs Vákár, “Principal Bundles and Gauge Theories,” arXiv:2110.06334**, full HTML https://arxiv.org/html/2110.06334. Read the relevant arguments in §§1.3.1, 2.1, 2.6.4, and 2.6.5. These support the right-principal/connection convention, gauge automorphism distinction, compactly supported variational setup, and source-free Yang–Mills equation. The thesis does not construct a quantum theory or replace the local proofs here.
+
+2. **Karl-Hermann Neeb, “Differential Topology of Fiber Bundles,” full lecture notes (2024)**, PDF https://www.math.fau.de/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bundle-lect.pdf. Read Chapter 5 §5.4 and Chapter 6 §6.1, including the connection-form gauge action, local section transition, Cartan curvature, and curvature descent argument. These support geometry and convention checks; they do not supply a Yang–Mills action or physical conclusion.
+
+3. **David Tong, “Gauge Theory,” full lecture notes, Chapter 2**, PDF https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/gauge-theory/gauge2.pdf. Read §§2.1.1–2.1.2, printed pp. 28–31 (PDF pp. 3–5). These state the natural-unit quadratic action, the classical equation, local gauge covariance, and the trace normalization convention. The displayed equation is a source check only; the author proof derives the variation and signs explicitly.
+
+## Item inventory, claims, and levels
+
+| Item | Level | In-run suppliers | Claim and convention |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| lem-qftx-su2-compact-nonabelian-invariant-form | 0 | none | Local mathematical supplier proving compactness/noncommutativity of the selected matrix group, the T_a basis and brackets, and the positive Ad-invariant trace form. It uses only mathematical inputs. |
+
+The next work is to author the model postulate, both assigned physics theorems, and substantial examples on the B page. The planned level calculation is: postulate 2 (batch-2 curvature and associated-derivative inputs are level 1); both theorems 3; a noncommuting action-density example 3; gauge and null-wave examples 4. Batch 19 itself remains at batch dependency level 1 from batch 2. Levels will be recomputed from the final exact manifest edges.
+
+## Current authoring checkpoint
+
+- Completed: lem-qftx-su2-compact-nonabelian-invariant-form, level 0. Its exact claim is compactness and noncommutativity of SU(2), the real basis T_a=-i sigma_a/2, the brackets [T_a,T_b]=epsilon_abc T_c, and kappa(X,Y)=-2 Tr_2(XY) with kappa(T_a,T_b)=delta_ab. It depends on ex-unitary-and-special-unitary-lie-groups, thm-heine-borel-rn, and def-countable-choice; all are mathematical. The compactness and trace-invariance computations are proved locally. Source references are the full Tong and Vákár texts above; their physics/geometry passages provide context, while the matrix, compactness, and positivity checks are proved in the carrier.
+- Completed: post-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model, level 2. It adopts Lorentzian M=R^(1,3), the exact global group SU(2), a selected right-principal bundle sector, empty matter content, kappa=-2 Tr_2 with kappa(T_a,T_b)=delta_ab, c=hbar=1, [A]=L^-1, [F]=L^-2, fixed dimensionless g_YM, and the local action -1/(2 g_YM^2) integral kappa(F wedge *F). Variations are smooth and compactly supported; no boundary values are imposed at infinity. The item depends on the inspected qftx geometry, qft-c01 units, exact gauge-group definition, and the local SU(2) matrix lemma. It does not depend on post-qft-constructed-model-and-measurement, because the model has no measurement or matter premise. Vákár §§1.3.1, 2.1, 2.6.5, Neeb Chapter 5 §5.4 and Chapter 6 §6.1, and Tong §2.1.1 support conventions and scope; the action remains an adopted postulate.
+- Completed: pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-classical-gauge-invariance, level 3. For a possibly nontrivial selected bundle it proves that a smooth equivariant bundle automorphism over the identity transports the connection and locally conjugates the curvature; the Ad-invariant trace pairing then gives pointwise density and action invariance. The local transition function is kept local, so the proof makes no global M-to-SU(2) identification. Direct suppliers are the model postulate, exact gauge-group/action definitions, the vertical-curvature transport proposition, the principal connection-form interface, the Cartan/Bianchi lemma, the associated-bundle interface, and the SU(2) invariant-form lemma. Vákár §2.1 and §2.6.5, Neeb Chapter 5 §5.4 / Chapter 6 §6.1, and Tong §2.1.2 were inspected; the bundle-action and trace-invariance arguments are complete in the carrier. Validation remains pending.
+- Completed: pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange, level 3. Its exact claim is stationarity under all smooth compactly supported local connection variations iff D_A(*F_A)=0 in every section, patched to the global adjoint-bundle equation. The local proof expands F_(A+epsilon a), obtains delta F=D_Aa, differentiates the relative action, proves the invariant-pairing covariant integration-by-parts identity, applies the choice-free compact-support integration lemma, and proves the converse coefficientwise using the scalar fundamental lemma. The overlap covariance is calculated from the actual right-action/Maurer–Cartan transition convention. Direct suppliers include the postulate, local Cartan/bracket/associated-bundle mathematics, the SU(2) form lemma, and lem-sr-compact-variation-and-fundamental-lemma. Vákár §§2.6.4–2.6.5, Neeb Chapter 5 §5.4 / Chapter 6 §6.1, and Tong §2.1.1 were inspected. No matter current is included or asserted. Validation remains pending.
+- Completed: ex-qftx-su2-noncommuting-yang-mills-action-density, level 3, on the B page. With the normalized basis and a nonzero inverse-length parameter it computes F=a^2 T_3 dx^1 wedge dx^2 and the nonzero Lorentzian quadratic action density. It explicitly makes no stationarity or field-equation claim. Dependencies are the postulate, local SU(2) matrix lemma, bracket definition, and curvature lemma. Tong §2.1.1 and Vákár §§1.3.1/2.6.5 were inspected; the commutator, Hodge-star sign, and action coefficient are verified in the example. Validation remains pending.
+- Completed: ex-qftx-su2-pure-gauge-yang-mills-action, level 3, on the B page. On the trivial bundle it changes the section by u=exp(T_3 sin(x^0/ell)), computes the nonzero local potential u^-1du, and verifies zero Cartan curvature and density. This is a classical section/gauge-description calculation, with no observation claim. Dependencies are the postulate, SU(2) matrix lemma, bracket definition, and curvature/transition lemma. Vákár §§1.3.1/2.1/2.6.5 and Tong §2.1.2 were inspected. Validation remains pending.
+- Completed: ex-qftx-su2-null-wave-yang-mills-solution, level 4, on the B page. For A=T_3 b sin((x^0-x^3)/ell) dx^1 it computes a nonzero null curvature, verifies D_A(*F)=0 with the stated Lorentzian Hodge convention, and applies the source-free Euler–Lagrange equivalence to conclude stationarity. It explicitly claims no uniqueness or empirical consequence. Dependencies are the postulate, SU(2) form lemma, bracket/curvature definitions, and the Euler–Lagrange theorem. Vákár §2.6.5 and Tong §2.1.1 were inspected. Validation remains pending.
+- Current validation: not run yet for the new item.
+- Unresolved prerequisites: none identified. The next action is to author the pure SU(2) model postulate with AC_omega carried only through its inspected mathematical geometry inputs, then the two conditional physical proofs and B-page examples.

