items/pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange.md:97:[A1] [[post-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model]]: $M$ has the fixed Minkowski metric and orientation in the Statement.
items/pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange.md:99:[A3] [[post-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model]]: the adopted action density is $-\kappa(F\wedge *_\eta F)/(2g_{\mathrm{YM}}^2)$.
items/pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange.md:101:[A4] [[post-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model]]: variations are smooth and compactly supported; no boundary values are imposed at infinity, and finite-region variations vanish near the boundary.
items/pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange.md:103:[F1] [[lem-qftx-su2-compact-nonabelian-invariant-form]]: $T_1,T_2,T_3$ are a basis of $\mathfrak{su}(2)$ with $\kappa(T_a,T_b)=\delta_{ab}$ and $\kappa$ is positive and $\operatorname{Ad}$-invariant.
items/pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange.md:105:[F2] [[def-qftx-principal-connection-form]] and [[lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi]]: local curvature is $F_i=dA_i+\frac12[A_i\wedge A_i]$, and the exterior covariant derivative is $D_{A_i}\eta=d\eta+[A_i\wedge\eta]$ with the graded bracket convention in the definition.
items/pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange.md:107:[F3] [[def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket]]: the bracket is graded skew and satisfies the graded derivation identity for the exterior derivative.
items/pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange.md:109:[F4] [[def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative]]: the adjoint representation gives local adjoint-bundle coordinates and the induced local covariant derivative.
items/pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange.md:111:[F5] [[lem-sr-compact-variation-and-fundamental-lemma]]: on an open Minkowski coordinate region, compactly supported $C^1$ coefficients admit differentiation under the integral sign and integration by parts; if a continuous scalar coefficient integrates to zero against every smooth compactly supported scalar test, it vanishes pointwise.
items/pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange.md:113:[F6] [[prop-adjoint-is-a-smooth-lie-group-representation]] and [[thm-the-differential-of-adjoint-is-ad]]: $\operatorname{Ad}$ is a smooth representation and its differential is $\operatorname{ad}$, so a varying local transition map differentiates by its Lie-algebra-valued Maurer–Cartan form.
